<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Fedsure adds a sparkle to yr share, div.</title>
<headline>Fedsure adds a sparkle to yr share, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		   126.9    vs   97.6</p>
<p>Div (cts)</p>
<p>    - interim		    35.5    vs   28.0</p>
<p>    - final			53.5    vs   41.5</p>
<p>    - total			89.0    vs   69.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	     133.1    vs   95.4</p>
<p>    Income after tax	  148.7    vs  111.0</p>
<p>Div payable April 11.</p>
<p>On register March 27.</p>
<p>Full name: Fedsure Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The directors said they were enthusiastic about future prospects, both for South Africa and for the Fedsure Group. They said the company was looking to further strengthen its core business and its positioning in the financial services and insurance industries, both in South Africa and abroad.</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters forecast year earnings per share on a range of 119.6 cents to 124.0 cents and a dividend on a range of 86.5 cents to 88.3 cents.</p>
<p>The consensus figures were earnings of 122.2 a share and a payout to shareholders of 87.0 cents a share.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
